<p>When a published article gets a fact wrong, we fix it on the article. We do not quietly delete it.</p>
<h2>What we correct</h2>
<p>A wrong result, name, time, title, date, or quote. A headline or summary the sources do not support. A label that no longer fits, such as a rumor the company has since confirmed or denied.</p>
<h2>How to ask</h2>
<p>Use the <a href="{{ '/contact/' | url }}">contact form</a>. Include the article URL, the passage, and a link to a source that shows the correct fact.</p>
<h2>What a correction looks like</h2>
<p>The article gets a note saying what was wrong and what it says now. The Last updated date changes. The original publication date stays.</p>
